  "worked_solution": "We factor the numerator and denominator, canceling out any common factors that appear in both.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{b}^{2}-7b+12}{4{b}^{2}+16b-84} & =\\frac{{b}^{2}-7b+12}{4({b}^{2}+4b-21)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(b-3)(b-4)}{4(b+7)(b-3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(b-3)}(b-4)}{4(b+7)\\cancel{(b-3)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{b-4}{4(b+7)} \\\\  & =\\frac{b-4}{4b+28}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
